QUALIFIER is released under the Zero-Clause BSD license (0BSD): no
attribution, no notice preservation, no conditions.

That covers the code written for this project: everything under main/, host/,
components/audio_hal, components/display, components/imu, the generator
tools/gen_z8002.py and tools/convert_roms.py, and the files core/polepos.c,
core/polepos.h, core/polepos_internal.h, core/polepos_video.c,
core/polepos_sound.c.

Two things carry their own terms, listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md:

  * core/z80/ is Marat Fayzullin's portable Z80 emulator. It is free for
    non-commercial use only and may not be distributed commercially. A build
    of this project therefore inherits that restriction.
  * core/z8000/z8002.c is a mechanical translation of MAME's Z8000 CPU core,
    and the board, video and sound models are written from MAME's Pole
    Position driver. MAME is BSD-3-Clause, which requires the copyright notice
    to be kept.

The Pole Position ROM images are not part of this project and are not
licensed by it. They remain the property of their copyright holders.

